# Git push / PR via GitHub App helper

`origin` SSH (deploy key) is **read-only**. Bare `git push`, `gh` (unauthenticated), or HTTPS without a token will fail with permission denied.

## When the user asks to push and/or open a PR

1. Create the local commit as usual (`git add` / `git commit`) — do **not** update git config; follow the usual commit safety rules.
2. Push + open/reuse PR with:

```bash
bash scripts/git_app_push.sh \
  --title "PR title" \
  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- …

## Test plan
- [ ] …
EOF
)"
```

Optional:

```bash
# Push only (no PR)
bash scripts/git_app_push.sh --no-pr

# Explicit feature branch name (still never main/master)
bash scripts/git_app_push.sh --branch feat/my-change --title "…" --body "…"

# Base branch (default: main)
bash scripts/git_app_push.sh --base main --title "…" --body "…"
```

3. Return the printed **PR:** URL (or the compare URL if PR create failed).

## Defaults / behavior

- Mints a short-lived GitHub App installation token (key default: `$HOME/.config/gh-app/retrotransposon-miner-vm-pusher.pem`).
- Pushes `HEAD` to a **writable** feature branch (default: timestamped `feat/<commit-subject-slug>--<stamp>`).
- Opens or reuses a PR into `main` (or `--base`).
- Never pushes directly to `main` / `master`. If `--branch` is protected, falls back to a fresh timestamped branch.
- Does **not** use `git push -u` with the tokenized URL (avoids storing the token in git config); sets upstream to `origin/<branch>` after push.

## Editing an existing PR title or body

`gh pr edit` fails here. The CLI queries classic Projects (`repository.pullRequest.projectCards`) and GitHub returns that GraphQL error. Update the PR with the REST API instead:

```bash
gh api -X PATCH repos/L1-Therapeutics/retrotransposon-miner/pulls/NUMBER \
  -f body="$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- …

## Test plan
- [ ] …
EOF
)"
```

`gh pr view` and `gh pr create` still work. Do not retry `gh pr edit` after the `projectCards` error. Details: `.cursor/skills/github-pr-edit/SKILL.md`.

## Do not

- Retry `git push origin HEAD` / `gh pr create` after deploy-key denial — use this script instead.
- Push to `main`/`master`.
- Print or commit the App private key or minted token.
